{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1404652-starting-a-new-pantheon-how-to-do-it","id":1404652,"title":"Starting a New Pantheon, How to do it.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-25T15:18:26-07:00","id":1404652,"title":"Starting a New Pantheon, How to do it.","content":"Historically, we know pantheons and the deities in them start somewhere. We know that Zeus and Hera started in different pantheons, Heracles got changed from being Hera's son/consort to her husband's bastard whom she hates. Set and Horus were once brothers, we have the stele to prove it. Indra once was the dominant God of India. The Loa, historically, were made up of deities from several African traditions. So, if the creation of new pantheons is part of real-world history, then there needs to be a way to do it in Scion.<br /> <br /> So, that said, I'll set up an example to speculate on. <br /> <br /> The planet was the first terraformable (at least in terms of what the ship's resources could offer) planet the lost ship found. They mis-jumped through warp-space and where hopelessly lost in both space and time. They also lacked the resources to repair the ship, if they could have even hoped to find a way home. Luckily for the people of the ship they had scions onboard. These Scions came from several different pantheons, but they agreed to put their differences aside to work for the survival of the passengers and crew. <br /> <br /> These Scions have severely limited communication with their patrons/parents. Still, they can receive birthrights and divine aid to advance.to godhood. So, stranded as the ship-folk are, they found a new society. A new society implies new traditions. So, how would they start their new pantheon once they have gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T18:10:47-07:00","id":1404683,"title":"","content":"Making a new Pantheon is definitely something that can be done in Scion.<br /> <br /> How, we don't know, and probably won't until the God book is out","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-26-2020, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T18:47:37-07:00","id":1404686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1404652-starting-a-new-pantheon-how-to-do-it?p=1404683#post1404683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a new Pantheon is definitely somethi g that can be done in Scion.<br /> <br /> How, we don't know, and probably won't until the God book is out</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not speculate on what might be done based on my example? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T00:20:03-07:00","id":1404717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1404652-starting-a-new-pantheon-how-to-do-it?p=1404686#post1404686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not speculate on what might be done based on my example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's not so much speculation on future mechanics in your case as much as it's 'Hey let's come up with examples for future characters who may want to make their own Pantheon' that is really a character exploration on what circumstances would make them want to form their own Pantheon, with blackjack and hookers. Such as an Aesir Scion who decided that Wyrd sucks ass and is throwing in her lot with her cross-Pantheon Band to escape her Wyrd by shedding her previous identity.<br /> <br /> Which, while an interesting character showcase, isn't something I've put a lot of thought into, as most of my character concepts probably won't go for Apotheosis and of those, most probably won't want to form their own Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T00:22:46-07:00","id":1404719,"title":"","content":"Okay the surviving Scions fatebound with one another, leading to developing co-dependant mantles at Demigod level (immortal tier). Their efforts to help the colony grow and thrive inspire the mortal survivors and when it clicks that these individuals are actual Scions, that is when actual cults begin to form.<br /> <br /> We are missing at least two books (Demigod and God) that we need for players to create a pantheon in game. We don't have the tools yet. I think that when this game was being developed one of the devs mentioned that when you create a pantheon in game, you retroactively add it to the World's history (I vaguely recall this was connected to the 'creation myth'). So maybe they find 'alien' ruined temples dedicated to their future mantles.<br /> <br /> Too many options, not enough information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}